# eBPF Exec Monitor

A lightweight eBPF-based process execution monitor built using **libbpf**. The program attaches to the Linux `execve` system call and reports every new process execution in real time.

## Features

- Monitors process execution using eBPF
- Captures:
  - Process ID (PID)
  - Parent Process ID (PPID)
  - Process name (`comm`)
  - Executable path
- Low-overhead kernel instrumentation
- User-space event handling with libbpf

## Architecture

```
          +----------------------+
          |   User Application   |
          |     execmon.c        |
          +----------+-----------+
                     |
               Ring Buffer
                     |
          +----------v-----------+
          |    eBPF Program      |
          |   execmon.bpf.c      |
          +----------+-----------+
                     |
           tracepoint/sys_enter_execve
                     |
          +----------v-----------+
          |     Linux Kernel     |
          +----------------------+
```

